{"name":"Aumbry","hex":"#7c7469","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aumbry","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of ambry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aumbry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ambry","blocks":[{"text":"An ambry is a recessed cabinet in the wall of a Christian church for storing sacred vessels and vestments. They are sometimes near the piscina, but more often on the opposite side. The word also seems in the Middle Ages for any closed cupboard or even a bookcase."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Langford_StMatthew_Aumbry.JPG/330px-Langford_StMatthew_Aumbry.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ambry","wikidata":"Q4821857"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/3HolyOils.jpg/500px-3HolyOils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/3HolyOils.jpg/1280px-3HolyOils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/3HolyOils.jpg/500px-3HolyOils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Catholic ambry containing vessels of the three holy oil: Chrism, Oil of catechumens, and the Oil of the Sick","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A3HolyOils.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Ambry_of_St_Mel%27s.jpg/500px-Ambry_of_St_Mel%27s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Ambry_of_St_Mel%27s.jpg/1280px-Ambry_of_St_Mel%27s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Ambry_of_St_Mel%27s.jpg/500px-Ambry_of_St